\paragraph{Critic convergence in pure imagination.}
Across all dual-critic configurations ($n{=}7$), critics converge ($\rho > 0.999$) with pessimism at 3--4\% of the independent-critic bound, rendering standard pessimistic estimation ineffective.

\paragraph{Wide dual-critic: the sole partial success.}
A $2{\times}2$ factorial (single/dual $\times$ narrow/wide) separates two mechanisms. \emph{Recovery}: narrow dual-critic (min-aggregation, ${\sim}1.2$M parameters) recovers from CIVO once it occurs (${\sim}16$--$19\times$ value-ratio reduction) but does not prevent onset. \emph{Prevention}: wide dual-critic (min $+$ ${\sim}2.4$M, $2\times$ capacity) achieves NVE $\leq 1.4\times$ in 3/4 seeds (3/3 Walker, 0/1 Cheetah)---the strongest result across all intervention levels (Table~\ref{tab:intervention_hierarchy}). Wide single-critic (capacity without min) shows 0/2 prevention, confirming both components are necessary. Cross-environment transfer is limited: the sole Cheetah seed exceeds prevention capacity (Appendix~\ref{sec:dual_critic_appendix}).

\paragraph{Why standard countermeasures fail.}
CIVO is an emergent property of trained temporal embeddings co-adapting with the world model, not a single-pathway defect---hence single-pathway post-hoc interventions are structurally insufficient. \emph{Gradient-level} (SGS): pathway redundancy means blocking any subset shifts co-adaptation to remaining channels (0/3 Cheetah elimination). \emph{Output-level} (RAVE): the EMA anchor tracks biased values during onset, violating its stationarity assumption. \emph{Representation-level} (TCN): binary on/off behavior suggests a phase transition, not continuous attenuation. The only reliable \emph{elimination}---freezing the embedding (0/16 controls)---reduces performance to 22--33\% of baseline (015b eval$=$204.2, 022b eval$=$300.7), destroying temporal conditioning capability entirely.

\paragraph{Why architectural intervention partially succeeds.}
The $2{\times}2$ critic factorial isolates two necessary components: min-aggregation alone enables \emph{recovery} (narrow dual, ${\sim}16$--$19\times$ ratio reduction) but not prevention; capacity alone (wide single) provides neither. Their combination---the minimum sufficient condition---achieves prevention in 3/4 seeds (NVE $\leq 1.4\times$). We hypothesize that increased capacity absorbs embedding-induced bias without propagating it to value targets, while the min operator provides a floor against catastrophic runaway. Incomplete Cheetah transfer (0/1, where CIVO severity reaches $70\times$) suggests a severity ceiling beyond which doubled capacity is insufficient. Variable-rate imagination in DreamerV3 remains an open problem; monitor via NVE ($\geq 2.0\times$; Table~\ref{tab:nve_loeo}). CIVO is specific to multi-joint locomotion (5/7 seeds; Appendix~\ref{sec:cross_env_appendix}).

